### Variables — VS Code REST Client (humao.rest-client)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@email = test@example.com
@password = password123

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health

### Register a new user
### Returns tokens + the user profile when SIGNUP_LOGIN=true (the default),
### or just the user profile when SIGNUP_LOGIN=false.
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "name": "Test User",
  "username": "testuser"
}

### Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Access token captured from the login response body
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.access_token}}
### (The refresh_token is returned in the `refresh_token` HttpOnly cookie and
###  sent automatically by the browser/REST Client on subsequent same-site calls.)

### Current user — GET /auth/me returns { "user": { ...profile } }
### Access token may be sent via the Authorization header (below) or the
### `access_token` cookie that login/register/refresh set on the browser.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Update the current user's profile (name / username)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User Updated",
  "username": "testuser2"
}

### Refresh tokens — POST /auth/refresh
### Uses the `refresh_token` cookie (sent automatically). Issues a new
### access_token (returned in the body) and rotates the refresh cookie.
# @name refresh
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh

### Logout — POST /auth/logout
### Sends the access token so the server can revoke it (jti denylist);
### also clears the access_token and refresh_token cookies.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Ingest a single document (JSON)
# @name ingest
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Rust Facts",
  "content": "Rust is a systems programming language that guarantees memory safety without a garbage collector, using an ownership system with borrowing and lifetimes.\n\nThe Rust compiler is called rustc, and the package manager is called Cargo. Packages in Rust are called crates and are published to crates.io.\n\nRust was originally created by Graydon Hoare at Mozilla Research, with the first stable release, Rust 1.0, shipping in May 2015."
}

### Ingest multiple documents at once (JSON array)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "title": "Doc A", "content": "The capital of France is Paris." },
  { "title": "Doc B", "content": "Water boils at 100 degrees Celsius at sea level." }
]

### Ingest raw text (title via query param; up to 10 MB per document)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/documents?title=Plain%20Doc
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: text/plain

Axum is a Rust web framework built on tokio and tower.

### Update a document (re-chunks and re-embeds atomically)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/documents/{{ingest.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Rust Facts v2",
  "content": "Rust 1.0 shipped in May 2015. The 2024 edition is the latest edition."
}

### List documents
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Delete a document
@documentId = {{ingest.response.body.id}}
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/documents/{{documentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Upload a file (multipart; add ?ingest=true to index text files for RAG)
# @name upload
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/files?ingest=true
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Notes uploaded from the frontend. The Golden Gate Bridge opened in 1937.
--WebAppBoundary--

### List uploaded files (shows ingestable + ingested status per file)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/files
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Ingest an already-uploaded file into the RAG index
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/files/{{upload.response.body.files.0.id}}/ingest
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Download a file
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/files/{{upload.response.body.files.0.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Delete a file
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/files/{{upload.response.body.files.0.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### RAG chat — ask a question about your documents
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Who created Rust and when was 1.0 released?"
}

### RAG chat with custom top_k
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "What is the Rust package manager called?",
  "top_k": 3
}
